<title>RUSSIA: Russian Duma votes to raise minimum wage.</title>
<headline>Russian Duma votes to raise minimum wage.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's State Duma lower house of parliament voted in a third reading on Friday to raise the minimum monthly wage by 10 percent to 83,490 roubles from January 1.</p>
<p>Few Russian workers are paid the minimum wage but it is an important benchmark for calculating public-sector pay, benefits, taxes and fines.</p>
<p>The minimum wage was last raised in April to 75,900 roubles from 63,250. Communist deputies and their allies have often pushed to index the wage to take into account inflation.</p>
<p>($=5,545 roubles)</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
